# HR Department DNS Configuration & Troubleshooting Lab

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates the configuration, testing, and troubleshooting of a DNS server in a simulated HR department network using Cisco Packet Tracer.

The lab uses a single local area network (LAN) with one router, one switch, one DNS server, five PCs, and five laptops.

The purpose of this project is to develop practical networking and IT Help Desk troubleshooting skills by configuring DNS, testing name resolution, deliberately creating a DNS failure, identifying the root cause, and restoring service.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

- Configure a basic LAN network.
- Configure static IP addresses.
- Configure a DNS server.
- Create DNS records.
- Test DNS name resolution.
- Use `nslookup` to troubleshoot DNS.
- Use `ping` to verify network connectivity.
- Identify an incorrect DNS server configuration.
- Correct the DNS configuration.
- Verify successful DNS resolution after the fix.
- Document the incident using ServiceNow.

