## 🧪 Testing

### Connectivity Testing

The devices were tested using `ping` to verify communication across the LAN.

Successful replies confirmed connectivity to the DNS server.

DNS Testing

DNS name resolution was tested using:

nslookup isaac.com

The DNS server successfully returned:

isaac.com → 192.168.10.10

The following command was also used:

ping isaac.com

Successful replies confirmed that the hostname could be resolved and reached.

🔧 DNS Troubleshooting Exercise

A DNS failure was deliberately introduced on Laptop 10.

The correct DNS server was:

192.168.10.10

The DNS configuration on Laptop 10 was changed incorrectly to:

192.168.10.99
Initial Test

The following command was executed:

nslookup isaac.com

Result:

DNS request timed out
🔍 Troubleshooting Process

The problem was isolated using a structured troubleshooting process.

1. Test the Default Gateway
ping 192.168.10.1

Result:

Reply

This confirmed that Laptop 10 had network connectivity.

2. Test the Actual DNS Server
ping 192.168.10.10

Result:

Reply

This confirmed that the DNS server was reachable.

3. Check DNS Configuration

The DNS server configured on Laptop 10 was found to be:

192.168.10.99

This was incorrect.

The correct DNS server was:

192.168.10.10
4. Correct the Configuration

The DNS server address was changed from:

192.168.10.99

to:

192.168.10.10
5. Verify the Fix

The following command was executed:

nslookup isaac.com

DNS resolution successfully returned the correct IP address.

📝 Root Cause

The root cause of the incident was an incorrect DNS server address configured on Laptop 10.

The laptop was configured to use:

192.168.10.99

instead of the correct DNS server:

192.168.10.10
✅ Resolution

The DNS server configuration on Laptop 10 was corrected to:

192.168.10.10

DNS resolution was then successfully verified using nslookup.

